  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "The product of a certain integer and nine more than that integer is 10. What can the integer be?\n\nIntroduce a pronumeral, write down a quadratic equation and solve it.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1$ or $-10$",
      "worked": "Let $n$ be the integer.\n$$\\begin{align*}n(n+9)&=10\\\\n^2+9n-10&=0\\\\(n+10)(n-1)&=0\\\\n+10&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad n-1=0\\\\n&=-10\\quad\\text{or}\\quad n=1\\end{align*}$$\nBoth roots are integers. The integer can be $1$ or $-10$.\n\nCheck: $1(1+9)=10$ and $(-10)(-10+9)=10$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 50
  },
